Z||000000||walsh2001||09-12-2001||09:25 AM||||I have heard that the MAT sensor can have a considerable efffect on engine performance... Is it common for them to wear out? What happens when they do? <P>Thanks, Jason<P>------------------<BR>'87 Fiero GT ... Cherry Red||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-12-2001||07:52 PM||||MAT problems are more common in 87-88 4 cylinder than V6.<P>Symptoms of a bad one can be very subtle or missleading. A bad one mainly throws of the fuel/air mix.<P>If yours is corroded or really filthy it's not a bad idea to just replace the thing. The one that's in there now is likely pretty old.<P>read the DIS notes in my cave for more info. (Note... unlike the 4 cylinder, the V6 uses the sensor with the metal cage. That one is more tolerant of the moisture common in the V6 air cleaner.)||||reg||1
